{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:18be9d6ece9a4cb2487124568b990f795211771fc7ec2009f69fcdfa06beeea6","title":"Can quantum fluctuations sustain self-reproduction in an assisted chaotic inflation model while the effective inflaton theory obeys a conjectured gravitational ultraviolet cutoff? The question concerns slow-roll eternal inflation rather than persistent expansion of metastable vacua.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:180fac21de16010157c65b0a8a1de2f4fe3a8cd798f6edc865da3cbc9956b032","title":"How do graviphoton gaugings and perturbative boundary superpotentials stabilize the radion and universal-hypermultiplet modulus, and which supersymmetric AdS stationary points support an uplift to a SUSY-breaking Minkowski vacuum?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0003"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18dc269a840e24c43184b7baeb0c1f289ceac9068875b176f09ea03c2b556f50","title":"Identify the ten-dimensional geometry behind a class of effective four-dimensional N=1 IIA AdS vacua, construct sources satisfying its RR two-form Bianchi identity, and exhibit a non-nearly-Kähler compactification within the same supersymmetry framework.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18c2d421b7bc1fccaa0b6047f5ca1f5b0d33b55edc4eced9a4f384aacce75f39","title":"How can nonlinear N=2 supersymmetry determine the off-shell magnetized D-brane effective action and its scalar potential, and under what additional conditions can its supersymmetric or supersymmetry-breaking vacua stabilize moduli?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:184595d5b60d76978dadc6a06c3fd9f7e5f84cd8ba056c25713c1a2cd088d526","title":"Can chiral gravity be extended supersymmetrically, with explicit gravitino modes and conserved charges demonstrating chirality and perturbative AdS3 stability under suitable boundary conditions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:188d6db23ffc93e21c63c1d2f3923e71b499f86faf2fe53e61c78ab3bffcc31a","title":"What obstructs string/M-theory compactification on internal manifolds with everywhere negative scalar curvature, and can warping, localized sources, conformal changes, or string corrections support such geometries relevant to de Sitter constructions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18a5e8212ad5a926d0d74e3d177808c9d0355569608ac3ebfa2c3dbc03554fd1","title":"Which bottom-up properties of CFT correlators guarantee a perturbative AdS effective field theory with a cutoff parametrically above the curvature scale, and what constraints follow for conserved higher-spin interactions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0013"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:186da3931017fddf28e82cb04ec8a81de3e2815d1d2a18599fc38542d9f7372a","title":"Does compactifying a positive-cosmological-constant higher-dimensional theory on multiple dynamical flux-supported spheres produce a distribution of lower-dimensional de Sitter vacua that accumulates at zero cosmological constant?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0015"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18e5c6073841daafeb51498312d23a4c8c2aafc5ed884a7fa985a4d6704021e7","title":"How does nonconstant warping determine the low-energy Kähler potential, holomorphic coordinates and kinetic terms of F-theory/IIB flux compactifications, including Kähler, universal, mobile-D3 and axionic moduli?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:185882e036f4b54e603fa4541e6d0d126a6a25ebe9b19dcd93193fdaeee81b93","title":"Can quantum gravity constrain massive gauge forces and discrete sectors strongly enough to restrict axion monodromy? The authors propose extending weak gravity beyond long-range forces.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18296467ff43e76121b3597a1fdf4faa24500b477ad93597abe9ffde742c681b","title":"How strongly can frequency-dependent arrival delays of fast radio bursts constrain a nonzero photon rest mass, and how does accounting for intergalactic plasma dispersion change the inferred upper limit?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:183c9f1446b31355bc42c1e12a69860a0e79235c4d7f464f30ff5405fbe48123","title":"Can post-inflationary fluctuations populate multiple minima of an axion-monodromy potential within one Hubble patch, and can subsequent bubble collisions generate an observable gravitational-wave signal?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18732ac980c7bf17b01e88f4c014fb2e3a4832fc8d34b32e54a5d7025539ca97","title":"Can the primordial spectrum predicted by perturbative holographic cosmology compete observationally with the ΛCDM power law, and can cosmological measurements discriminate among the proposed three-dimensional dual QFTs?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18b4570912a41a8b098f5e1a31e7b7c07447ce7ba16195b63271520ff48d974e","title":"Could naturally ultralight bosons alter neutrino-scale Casimir vacua? Axions provide motivated masses near or below neutrino thresholds, with additional classical energy possible in winding sectors.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0025"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:183c1144cd69e18768d12aad92cf84c1f3bcf74afdae614184e3d68b2260ad63","title":"Can logarithmic perturbative corrections to the Kähler potential, combined with magnetic D7-brane D-terms, stabilize geometric Kähler moduli at a de Sitter vacuum without nonperturbative superpotential effects?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1894873013d24e6b4892308ac59d64486b2efbb93fe002f06614dd16c8d2331a","title":"Can altered degrees of freedom, kinetic terms, initial states, or conjectural criteria evade the conventional scalar-power argument?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18e6b118e8e5b947204bd0483aede08ea42e9b93fbe8e8fc68b8ef1a7818389d","title":"Does the selected scalar sector reveal a tachyon in every classical de Sitter solution with intersecting sources?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1834f4b5e0ec8ae541bf2af110d283008c3197872ea91eb59958386dca077eb9","title":"How do Hawking emission and electric-field pair production jointly determine the emission of one charged particle species from a charged black hole, including near-extremal limits? Extremal-black-hole decay and the weak gravity conjecture motivate the question; the conjecture is not derived.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:185ac8d73d64d28130a2008434e05b4be603a2c03aeea7a61f298708e915bba1","title":"Euclidean wormholes can introduce spacetime-independent coupling labels, whereas higher-dimensional quantum gravity is expected to have no freely adjustable parameters. The paper asks whether topology-changing quantum redundancies can reconcile these claims without replacing a single holographic boundary theory by an ensemble.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:180df4033cd3769bba367aa1af71630b25f80329f70d8f18fe4e1c029e1609a9","title":"Can four-dimensional de Sitter spacetime be constructed in string theory as a coherent state over a supersymmetric Minkowski background, while addressing quantum stability, trans-Planckian obstructions, vacuum energy and finite entropy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1855f178ebefa6ff458e84089bf9598a8636ed2a74375147a20ef544a42b0d16","title":"How can a thermal conformal state carry spontaneous order? The order parameter scales as T^Δ, while energy density, pressure, and entropy obey the conformal equation of state without an independent dimensionful deformation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1832377ac80c47771929ebd537c49b95192137e513de515653d4c8e6012ef216","title":"Can scalar derivative backgrounds or vector condensation replace physical F- or D-term expectation values as sources of spontaneous SUSY breaking, while producing accelerated expansion and visible-sector mass splitting?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18678dad163640aab831bb0c71349ff32ffe6b76644f5429f24e9d826769f33d","title":"Does the model have excitations at the AdS curvature scale and a tower becoming light as the cosmological constant vanishes? The source compares its scalar Hessian and proposed higher-spin modes with conjectural bounds normally motivated by other gravitational effective theories.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0067"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:181b7d72d1bae7952e88eee6df7edecaa835680729f61040731ceedfdea9a4b9","title":"Which AdS region makes an entropy comparison sensitive to the cosmological scale? The paper fixes the box radius at order the AdS radius, between locally flat small spheres and large spheres with comparable area-volume growth.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0070"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:182ce637bc310352a4e6a46a40d89156c53c8fbad84f67374a40712d3c20caa4","title":"Can nilpotent Kähler corrections realize universal inflationary attractors and small positive vacuum energy without requiring a supersymmetric-AdS precursor, while satisfying the gradient de Sitter conjecture?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0075"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1823e6ba86f6d096b6fb369bfee23355af47c2a348da41a402a3c1362c2d511d","title":"How do classical, volume-modulus kination runaways in a lower-dimensional EFT map to higher-dimensional cosmologies, and what do their asymptotics suggest about dynamical Swampland constraints?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0079"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18e9c2626a6ba3fa6afe5b24c7d3a067534e6947d8d3feb6da7ac46bd04568db","title":"Can modular bootstrap determine BPS-string elliptic genera, including gauge-instanton strings, in 6d supergravity, and can these spectra test Swampland conjectures in theories lacking F-theory realizations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0084"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1877ac824b12f923a22b9a1410a474675bcab4fcc7fee2a93c55f9d96742d23a","title":"How do nonlinear electromagnetic interactions modify electrically and magnetically charged black holes, including their geometry, thermodynamics, geodesics, regularity, holographic applications, and proposed quantum-gravity constraints?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0090"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1871e0b76f84078a00be7f328c49e040fab6590092cf12f960c1947de43ddcbe","title":"How do duality monodromies constrain bordisms between circle-compactified gravitational theories, and can unbounded commutator width require more duality defects than ordinary first-bordism trivialization demands?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0100"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:185890ed31ca328f4c38953e8e32828192ce6ed8c7995ee1ed76433f5adfaf00","title":"Does the growth of central charge between neighboring CFTs constrain the single-trace higher-spin gap, and what structure distinguishes physical families from arbitrary sequences? Motivations include canonical central-charge scalings, bounded gaps in vector models, and the validity of semiclassical AdS gravity.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0102"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:18eb938a5ac4cc33b7e2ef60ce8e8b89272a9387e1070e154eb0c2d1b94f6031","title":"Can a holographically constrained vacuum energy with a cosmological infrared cutoff describe a variable, true cosmological constant while respecting gravitational conservation identities and the observational requirements discussed in the paper?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0103"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1850acba4e12587180b0636cb376e5c674e283e6140cec1d4a7914d8267a476f","title":"Does gravitational false-vacuum decay possess the negative fluctuation mode needed for a decay interpretation, and why do different reductions to one physical variable give different answers?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0104"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:186f00227b632738ef2273c7a53239f0a3007abd22f83763e719ef3128d24ba2","t